r2 commit message (2433 chars):
KS-1239 LEGDPINS: move LEG D's three index.ts line pins by the -18 this PR causes

Round 2 of 2. The tier-1 gate's one blocker, and nothing else.

packages/shared's LEG D leg - in ks781-p3-3-body-parser-order.test.ts - pins
three api-gateway src/index.ts sites BY
LINE NUMBER. This PR removes 18 lines above all three, so they move and the
shared suite reds 915/917 at this head and merged - deterministically, not
flakily. LEG D is the only place that list lives, and it lives in a DIFFERENT
package from the one this PR touches, which is why my own lane run could not
see it: api-gateway went 742 -> 746 green while packages/shared went red.

Measured here, each new line read back out of the file rather than taken from
the gate's mail or re-baselined from a run - the discipline this file's own
comments require:

  845 -> 827  app.post('/api/auth/wallet/challenge', mockBodyParser, ...
  858 -> 840  app.post('/api/auth/wallet/authenticate', mockBodyParser, ...
  873         the createVerificationRoutes factory argument (was 891)

A uniform -18 on all three, with the same `via`, matching this PR's +0/-18.
index.ts 1279 -> 1261.

Four edits carry that: the three strings in LEG D's toEqual list, and the
CONTROL cell's toContain, which pins the factory-argument site by number too.
Two adjacent comments named the old numbers as the live ones and would have
been stale the moment the pins moved, so they are brought in line in the same
commit - that kind of stale comment is exactly what bit this round already.
A read-back note is added in the shape the five previous instances of this
move use; the file asks for it in as many words.

The pins are still NUMBERS. Pinning by text instead is a design change to
another ticket's guard and is NOT done here; it is raised as a proposal in the
READY instead.

Proven at this head, serially: packages/shared 917/917 green, 0 red, over 205
files; api-gateway 746/746; tsc --noEmit rc 0 with 0 errors in both packages.
Note for whoever reads a failing run of this suite: a parallel run of
packages/shared on a loaded machine reds four whole-repo WALKING guards
(crypto-agility, entrypoint-corpus, ks764 revoke call sites, ks860 listeners)
with STACK_TRACE_ERROR and no assertion text. That is contention, not the
tree - each of the four is green run alone, and the whole suite is green with
--no-file-parallelism.

Refs KS-1239

